Bound binary trie/CIDR lengths and allocate only for decoded elements.
Inspired by the binary reader hardening in Citrus PR #16:
https://github.com/getmikan/Citrus/pull/16

Keep the existing binary format and error paths. Bound trie element counts to
2^28 and CIDR range counts to 2^26. Append successfully decoded elements rather
than preallocating an array from a file header. Read label bytes through a
LimitedReader and check that the full declared payload was available.

This focused change covers DomainSet, DomainMap and IpCidrSet readers.
Regression tests cover length bounds, overflow panics, bounded allocation for
short inputs, matching, byte-for-byte round trips and reader boundaries.

